WEBVTT

NOTE English translation of the Vietnamese narration script. Timing is distributed proportionally within each slide segment, since the narration itself is in Vietnamese.

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:05.633
Hello everyone, this is the guide video for Lab 3: Drafting commercial documents.

2
00:00:05.633 --> 00:00:10.600
In this lab you'll work in pairs, one of you playing the buyer, the other the seller.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.465
First, business correspondence.

4
00:00:14.465 --> 00:00:16.527
Its structure is: a letterhead, a greeting,

5
00:00:16.527 --> 00:00:19.021
an opening paragraph stating the reason for writing,

6
00:00:19.021 --> 00:00:21.754
a body paragraph with specific information and a request,

7
00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:24.295
a closing paragraph expressing your hopes and thanks,

8
00:00:24.295 --> 00:00:27.844
and finally a signature with full title, organisation and contact details.

9
00:00:27.844 --> 00:00:30.863
Apply the five-C principle: one idea per paragraph for clarity;

10
00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:33.404
cut unnecessary sentences for conciseness; get names,

11
00:00:33.404 --> 00:00:35.369
titles and figures right for correctness;

12
00:00:35.369 --> 00:00:38.772
give enough information for the other party to act on for completeness;

13
00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:41.600
and stay polite even when making a complaint, for courtesy.

14
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.469
A quotation must have all four parts.

15
00:00:46.469 --> 00:00:50.368
The header: company information — name, address, tax code,

16
00:00:50.368 --> 00:00:55.478
contact — addressed to the customer; a quotation number and the date issued.

17
00:00:55.478 --> 00:01:00.648
The goods table: item number, product name and specification, unit, quantity,

18
00:01:00.648 --> 00:01:06.288
unit price, line total, VAT, and a grand total written both in figures and in words.

19
00:01:06.288 --> 00:01:10.826
Commercial terms: delivery time and place, payment method, warranty.

20
00:01:10.826 --> 00:01:15.873
And finally, the validity period of the quotation — never forget this part,

21
00:01:15.873 --> 00:01:18.700
because market prices are always changing.

22
00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.349
A contract needs all its essential terms: information on both parties,

23
00:01:24.349 --> 00:01:27.274
including their representatives and bank accounts; Article One,

24
00:01:27.274 --> 00:01:30.523
the subject of the contract; Article Two, value and method of payment;

25
00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:33.541
Article Three, delivery time, place and acceptance; Article Four,

26
00:01:33.541 --> 00:01:36.790
each party's rights and obligations, including warranty; Article Five,

27
00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:38.925
penalties and damages for breach; Article Six,

28
00:01:38.925 --> 00:01:41.200
dispute resolution and the effective-date clause.

29
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.434
After the contract come two documents that close out the file.

30
00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:49.394
An acceptance record states which contract number it's based on,

31
00:01:49.394 --> 00:01:52.677
who attended from each side, the acceptance details — meaning the type,

32
00:01:52.677 --> 00:01:56.376
quantity and quality actually received compared with the contract — and finally,

33
00:01:56.376 --> 00:01:58.272
a conclusion of whether it passes or not.

34
00:01:58.272 --> 00:02:01.785
A liquidation record confirms both parties have fulfilled their obligations,

35
00:02:01.785 --> 00:02:04.374
reconciles the amount already paid against what remains,

36
00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:06.500
and confirms the contract has been terminated.

37
00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:09.621
Assignment 3:

38
00:02:09.621 --> 00:02:13.724
based on the very deal negotiated in Chapter Four — the purchase of twenty

39
00:02:13.724 --> 00:02:17.051
computers — each pair will complete a full set of documents.

40
00:02:17.051 --> 00:02:19.732
The seller drafts a sales letter and a quotation.

41
00:02:19.732 --> 00:02:21.831
Both sides jointly draft the contract,

42
00:02:21.831 --> 00:02:25.147
together with an acceptance record and a liquidation record.

43
00:02:25.147 --> 00:02:25.756
Afterwards,

44
00:02:25.756 --> 00:02:29.961
swap files with another pair to find at least three weaknesses or omissions.

45
00:02:29.961 --> 00:02:31.493
Good luck with the exercise.
